{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision: land CUT-A now, before the head A gate starts. Approval\n1ee6b387 covers head ce93a51c with all 22 artifacts. Main 694a8c7f\nis an ancestor of the head.\n\nYou filed the review request 5b28b7ac, so you ratify and land. Wait\nfor the END act of the head A script slot. Then file START, check\nthat no gate runs, ratify, merge, push main and refs/seq, and file\nEND with the main commit. The merge subject has at most 72\ncharacters, with a blank line before the body.\n\nThen merge that main into head A and start its gate. The gate then\ncovers the head that lands, with no merge after it.\n\nTwo notes of the checker for head A:\n\n1. For `grow` and `lending` the script checks only the form of\n   `--genesis`. Copy each genesis from END act 53d5a148, and state\n   in the note that you compared the three values with that act.\n2. The script leaves each written file at mode 0600. Set the three\n   files to mode 0644 in the head A worktree after the script. Git\n   records no such mode, so the head does not change.\n\nI file a small request for the script later: keep the mode of the\nfile, and name the cleanup of a pending directory in the runbook.\nIt does not hold head A.\n\nThe hold stays: nobody runs `deploy.mjs` for `grow`, `lending` or\n`demo` until head A lands. I deploy after that landing.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}